---The properties of the price sheet.
---@class azure.cost_management.MCAPriceSheetProperties
---@field billingAccountID? string Unique identifier for the billing account.
---@field billingAccountName? string Name of the billing profile that is set up to receive invoices. The prices in the price sheet are associated with this billing profile.
---@field billingProfileId? string Unique identifier for the billing profile.
---@field billingProfileName? string Name of the billing profile that is set up to receive invoices. The prices in the price sheet are associated with this billing profile.
---@field productOrderName? string Name of the purchased product plan. Indicates if this pricing is standard Azure Plan pricing, Dev/Test pricing etc. Currently unavailable for Azure 3rd party and ReservedInstance meters.
---@field serviceFamily? number Type of Azure service. For example, Compute, Analytics, and Security.
---@field product? string Name of the product accruing the charges.
---@field productId? string Unique identifier for the product whose meter is consumed.
---@field skuId? string Unique identifier of the SKU
---@field unitOfMeasure? string How usage is measured for the service
---@field meterId? string Unique identifier of the meter
---@field meterName? string Name of the meter. The meter represents the deployable resource of an Azure service.
---@field meterType? string Name of the meter type
---@field meterCategory? string Name of the classification category for the meter. For example, Cloud services, Networking, etc.
---@field meterSubCategory? string Name of the meter subclassification category.
---@field meterRegion? string Name of the Azure region where the meter for the service is available.
---@field tierMinimumUnits? string Defines the lower bound of the tier range for which prices are defined. For example, if the range is 0 to 100, tierMinimumUnits would be 0.
---@field effectiveStartDate? string Effective start date of the Price Sheet billing period
---@field effectiveEndDate? string Effective end date of the Price Sheet billing period
---@field unitPrice? string The per-unit price at the time of billing for a given product or service, inclusive of any negotiated discounts on top of the market price. For PriceType ReservedInstance, unit price reflects the total cost of the 1 or 3-year commitment including discounts. Note: The unit price isn't the same as the effective price in usage details downloads when services have differential prices across tiers. If services have multi-tiered pricing, the effective price is a blended rate across the tiers and doesn't show a tier-specific unit price. The blended price or effective price is the net price for the consumed quantity spanning across the multiple tiers (where each tier has a specific unit price).
---@field basePrice? string The unit price at the time the customer signs on or the unit price at the time of service meter GA launch if it is after sign-on. This is applicable for Enterprise Agreement users
---@field marketPrice? string The current list price for a given product or service. This price is without any negotiations and is based on your Microsoft Agreement type. For PriceType Consumption, market price is reflected as the pay-as-you-go price. For PriceType Savings Plan, market price reflects the Savings plan benefit on top of pay-as-you-go price for the corresponding commitment term. For PriceType ReservedInstance, market price reflects the total price of the 1 or 3-year commitment.
---@field currency? string Currency in which all the prices are reflected.
---@field billingCurrency? string Currency in which charges are posted.
---@field term? string Term length for Azure Savings Plan or Reservation term – one year or three years (P1Y or P3Y)
---@field priceType? string Price type for a product. For example, an Azure resource with a pay-as-you-go rate with priceType as Consumption. Other price types include ReservedInstance and Savings Plan.

---The properties of the benefit recommendation when scope is 'ManagementGroup'.
---@class azure.cost_management.ManagementGroupScopeBenefitRecommendationProperties
---@field firstConsumptionDate? string The first usage date used for looking back for computing the recommendations.
---@field lastConsumptionDate? string The last usage date used for looking back for computing the recommendations.
---@field lookBackPeriod? azure.cost_management.LookBackPeriod The number of days of usage evaluated for computing the recommendations.
---@field totalHours? number The total hours for which the cost is covered. Its equal to number of records in a property 'properties/usage/charges'.
---@field usage? azure.cost_management.RecommendationUsageDetails On-demand charges between firstConsumptionDate and lastConsumptionDate that were used for computing benefit recommendations.
---@field armSkuName? string ARM SKU name. 'Compute_Savings_Plan' for SavingsPlan.
---@field term? azure.cost_management.Term Term period of the benefit. For example, P1Y or P3Y.
---@field commitmentGranularity? azure.cost_management.Grain Grain of the proposed commitment amount. Supported values: 'Hourly'
---@field currencyCode? string An ISO 4217 currency code identifier for the costs and savings amounts.
---@field costWithoutBenefit? number The current cost without benefit, corresponds to 'totalHours' in the look-back period.
---@field recommendationDetails? azure.cost_management.AllSavingsBenefitDetails The details of the proposed recommendation.
---@field allRecommendationDetails? azure.cost_management.AllSavingsList The list of all benefit recommendations with the recommendation details.
---@field scope azure.cost_management.ManagementGroupScopeBenefitRecommendationPropertiesScope Benefit scope. For example, Single or Shared.
---@field managementGroupId? string Fully-qualified identifier of the management group that this management group scope recommendation is for, of the format /providers/Microsoft.Management/managementGroups/{managementGroupId}. Applicable only if recommendation is for 'ManagementGroup' scope.
---@field tenantId? string The tenant ID associated with the management group. Populated only when managementGroupId is populated.

