---Savings plan utilization summary resource.
---@class azure.cost_management.SavingsPlanUtilizationSummary
---@field id? string Fully qualified resource ID for the resource. E.g. "/subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroupName}/providers/{resourceProviderNamespace}/{resourceType}/{resourceName}"
---@field name? string The name of the resource
---@field type? string The type of the resource. E.g. "Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines" or "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"
---@field systemData? azure.cost_management.SystemData Azure Resource Manager metadata containing createdBy and modifiedBy information.
---@field kind azure.cost_management.SavingsPlanUtilizationSummaryKind Supported values: 'SavingsPlan'.
---@field properties? azure.cost_management.SavingsPlanUtilizationSummaryProperties Savings plan utilization summary properties.

---Supported values: 'SavingsPlan'.
---@alias azure.cost_management.SavingsPlanUtilizationSummaryKind "SavingsPlan"

---Savings plan utilization summary properties.
---@class azure.cost_management.SavingsPlanUtilizationSummaryProperties
---@field armSkuName? string ARM SKU name. For example, 'Compute_Savings_Plan' for savings plan.
---@field benefitId? string The benefit ID is the identifier of the benefit.
---@field benefitOrderId? string The benefit order ID is the identifier for a benefit purchase.
---@field benefitType? azure.cost_management.BenefitKind The benefit type. Supported values: 'SavingsPlan'.
---@field usageDate? string Date corresponding to the utilization summary record. If the grain of data is monthly, value for this field will be first day of the month.
---@field avgUtilizationPercentage? number This is the average hourly utilization for each date range that corresponds to given grain (Daily, Monthly). Suppose the API call is for usageDate > 2025-03-01 and usageDate < 2022-10-31 at a daily granularity. There will be one record per benefit id for each day. For a single day, the avgUtilizationPercentage value will be equal to the average of the set of values where the set contains 24 utilization percentage entries one for each hour in a specific day.
---@field minUtilizationPercentage? number This is the minimum hourly utilization for each date range that corresponds to given grain (Daily, Monthly). Suppose the API call is for usageDate > 2025-03-01 and usageDate < 2022-10-31 at a daily granularity. There will be one record per benefit id for each day. For a single day, the minUtilizationPercentage value will be equal to the smallest in the set of values where the set contains 24 utilization percentage entries one for each hour in a specific day. If on the day 2022-10-18, the lowest utilization percentage was 10% at hour 4, then the value for the minUtilizationPercentage in the response will be 10%.
---@field maxUtilizationPercentage? number This is the maximum hourly utilization for each date range that corresponds to given grain (Daily, Monthly). Suppose the API call is for usageDate > 2025-03-01 and usageDate < 2022-10-31 at a daily granularity. There will be one record per benefit id for each day. For a single day, the maxUtilizationPercentage value will be equal to the largest in the set of values where the set contains 24 utilization percentage entries one for each hour in a specific day. If on the day 2022-10-18, the largest utilization percentage was 90% at hour 5, then the value for the maxUtilizationPercentage in the response will be 90%.

